Carried patch, Windows only: LIBXSMM's POWER generator under LLP64.

LIBXSMM 2.1.0's ppc64le generator holds 64-bit instruction words, immediates
and offsets in long and unsigned long, which are 32 bits on Windows. GCC fails
with -Werror=overflow on the prefixed instruction constants, with a duplicate
case label when a 64-bit form index truncates to 0, and with
-Werror=shift-count-overflow in libxsmm_ppc64le_instr_set_imm64, which shifts
its argument by 32 and 48. This widens every long in the POWER generator
(and four casts at its call sites in generator_spgemm_csr_asparse_reg.c) to
long long, and one %ld to %lld to match. The code never runs on x86; it is still
compiled. The types are the same width on LP64, so nothing changes there.
Still present in 2.1.0, the tag Palace 0.19.0 pins.

